    "source": "Recorded with tee-cli.ts in front of `agy acp` 1.5.15, driven by ADE CORE's ACP backend in a throwaway git folder. `frames`: `session/load` of the session agy 1.5.15 made in the MCP turn capture; agy replays both turns (user_message_chunk, tool_call with its final status, agent_message_chunk, usage_update) in the 2 ms before it answers, with no marker on the replayed frames, then answers with models, modes and config options and sends `session_info_update` with the title after the answer. `resume`: `session/resume` of the same session answers after about a second with no replay, then `session_info_update`. `load141`: `session/load` of a session the 1.4.1 server made in the same folder answers -32002 \"Session not found\" after 6.2 s; `resume141`: `session/resume` of it answers -32603 \"Failed to read session ...; retry, or load it with session/load\". A 1.4.1 session does not carry over to 1.5. Thought chunks are left out, consecutive message chunks are merged into one and the model list is cut to two. `t` is milliseconds from the start of each process.",
